# Integer operations proven inside the safe integers by intervals (note/term/codegen/passes.md, P2). Every `+`, `-`
# and `*` on two numbers is checked on every backend, because a result past the range is a different integer or a
# rounded one. A check whose operands are bounded can never fire, and this fact names the operations where that is
# proven, so an emitter writes them plain; and a `/` or `%` whose divisor is proven not zero (nor -1 for a quotient of
# an unknown, the one quotient that overflows).
#
# Two levels, solved together. IN A TASK, FLOW-SENSITIVE: each task is walked forward with a state of intervals for
# its locals, an `if` refining each branch by its condition and joining after, a `while` iterated to a fixpoint (widened
# after a few turns, then narrowed once), a guard's handler starting with every name its body assigns unknown, and a
# closure seeing only the names that never change. ACROSS THE PROGRAM, A FIXPOINT of what the walks find: the
# parameters of a task only the program calls, the answers of a task defined once, the slots of a list a record owns,
# and the number fields of a plain record. A task whose walk takes more than its step budget proves nothing.
#
# Ported from ir/facts/interval.ts (self-hosting, 2026-10-06), which stays as the face and says why each rule is shaped
# as it is. The decisions:
#   - THE ORIGINAL KEYS ITS FACTS BY NODE IDENTITY: what each node gives a global, and what each expression evaluated to.
#     Term has none, so a node is its place in compile/node-reach.tree's walk of its task's body, with `type` and `span`
#     skipped as the original's every walk skipped them: `order`, statements and expressions interleaved. The walk
#     carries each node's place, a child's place being its parent's plus the sizes of the subtrees before it, each size
#     read off node-reach (`extent`) so the order is node-reach's alone. The answer is the proven nodes themselves, the
#     same objects on TypeScript, and the face makes the `WeakSet`
#   - A PLACE IS NOT AN IDENTITY where the program shares a node: a compiled program does (an inlined task's body shares
#     its literals with every copy and with the task's own body), and the original read one value recorded for the
#     object wherever it stood, so a copy that never runs proved a divisor another copy recorded. So the face hands in
#     each place's identity, the first place across every task that holds the same object (`ids`), and what a node
#     gives and what it evaluated to are kept by identity. The pairing found it: a `% 100` the original proved and the
#     place alone did not
#   - every reflective walk of the original (the static scan, a stored local's elements, the names a guard's body
#     assigns, the names a closure writes, the names read as values) is a pass over that order. A closure's subtree is
#     the places from it up to its size, and a call's callee is the place after the call
#   - an interval is `span-value`: `no-value` the original's `null`, `any-value` its `'top'`, `within` a pair of floats.
#     Infinity is `1.0 / 0.0` and every operation on the floats is JavaScript's, so `Infinity - Infinity` is NaN and
#     `make-span` turns it into `any-value` as `span` did
#   - a walk over budget threw `Spent` out of the walk. Here it sets `spent`, after which every evaluation answers at
#     once and every loop stops: what the rest of that walk would write is never read, since a spent task gives
#     `any-value` to every global it reaches and is never asked for a proof
#   - `list_push` handed one argument made the original throw (a `WeakMap` key of `undefined`). Here it gives nothing.
#     The checker gives every `list_push` two

load @term/base/list
  find list
  find get
  find contains

load @term/base/maybe
  find maybe

load @term/base/text
  find split
  find substring

load @term/base/float
  find to-decimal
  find is-not-a-number
  find is-finite

load ../../compile/node
  find expression
  find expression-type
  find statement
  find type
  find binding
  find method-of

load ../../compile/node-reach
  find reached
  find reach-statements
  find reach-expression

load ../../compile/lowered-members
  find list-length-tasks

# ---- the constants ----

# the largest safe integer, 2^53 - 1: a side past it is infinite
task safe-limit
  like float
  mark private

  back 9007199254740991.0

task infinity
  like float
  mark private

  back divide(1.0, 0.0)

task minus-infinity
  like float
  mark private

  back subtract(0.0, infinity())

# rounds a global may grow before the side that grows is widened
task widen-rounds
  like number
  mark private

  back 16

# turns a loop may grow before the side that grows is widened
task widen-turns
  like number
  mark private

  back 6

# the steps one task's walk may take in one round before it gives up
task step-budget
  like number
  mark private

  back 400000

# ---- intervals ----

# what an expression may evaluate to: nothing (unreachable, or the fixpoint's bottom), any value, or a range whose sides
# may be infinite, which is unknown on that side only
form span-value
  case no-value
  case any-value
  case within
    link lo, like float
    link hi, like float

task nothing
  like span-value
  mark private

  back make no-value

task anything
  like span-value
  mark private

  back make any-value

task lesser
  take a, like float
  take b, like float
  like float
  mark private

  fork test, is-below(b, a)
    hold
      back b
  back a

task greater
  take a, like float
  take b, like float
  like float
  mark private

  fork test, is-above(b, a)
    hold
      back b
  back a

task absolute-of
  take a, like float
  like float
  mark private

  fork test, is-below(a, 0.0)
    hold
      back subtract(0.0, a)
  back a

# a range, a side past the safe integers infinite, and both sides infinite (or either not a number) any value
task make-span
  take lo, like float
  take hi, like float
  like span-value
  mark private

  fork test, or(is-not-a-number(lo), is-not-a-number(hi))
    hold
      back make any-value
  save low, lo
  fork test, is-below(lo, subtract(0.0, safe-limit()))
    hold
      save low, minus-infinity()
  save high, hi
  fork test, is-above(hi, safe-limit())
    hold
      save high, infinity()
  fork test, and(is-equal(low, minus-infinity()), is-equal(high, infinity()))
    hold
      back make any-value
  back
    make within
      bind lo, low
      bind hi, high

# a range with both sides known, the only kind that proves anything
task finite
  take v, like span-value
  like boolean
  mark private

  sift v
    case within
      link lo
      link hi
      back and(is-finite(lo), is-finite(hi))
    miss
      back false

task is-no-value
  take v, like span-value
  like boolean
  mark private

  sift v
    case no-value
      back true
    miss
      back false

task join-values
  take a, like span-value
  take b, like span-value
  like span-value
  mark private

  sift a
    case no-value
      back b
    case any-value
      sift b
        case no-value
          back a
        miss
          back make any-value
    case within
      link a-lo
      link a-hi
      sift b
        case no-value
          back a
        case any-value
          back make any-value
        case within
          link b-lo
          link b-hi
          back
            make within
              bind lo, lesser(a-lo, b-lo)
              bind hi, greater(a-hi, b-hi)

task same-values
  take a, like span-value
  take b, like span-value
  like boolean
  mark private

  sift a
    case no-value
      back is-no-value(b)
    case any-value
      sift b
        case any-value
          back true
        miss
          back false
    case within
      link a-lo
      link a-hi
      sift b
        case within
          link b-lo
          link b-hi
          back and(is-equal(a-lo, b-lo), is-equal(a-hi, b-hi))
        miss
          back false

# the side of `after` that grew past `before`, widened to unknown
task widen
  take before, like span-value
  take after, like span-value
  like span-value
  mark private

  sift before
    case within
      link before-lo
      link before-hi
      sift after
        case within
          link after-lo
          link after-hi
          save lo, after-lo
          fork test, is-below(after-lo, before-lo)
            hold
              save lo, minus-infinity()
          save hi, after-hi
          fork test, is-above(after-hi, before-hi)
            hold
              save hi, infinity()
          back make-span(lo, hi)
        miss
          back after
    miss
      back after

# a product's corner. An unknown side times 0 is 0, since what it stands for is a number
task times
  take x, like float
  take y, like float
  like float
  mark private

  fork test, or(is-equal(x, 0.0), is-equal(y, 0.0))
    hold
      back 0.0
  back multiply(x, y)

# the arithmetic of two intervals, by operator, and any value for an operator this does not track
task arith
  take op, like text
  take a, like span-value
  take b, like span-value
  like span-value
  mark private

  # a remainder by a divisor that excludes zero is smaller than the divisor, whatever the dividend
  fork test, is-equal(op, <%>)
    hold
      sift b
        case within
          link d-lo
          link d-hi
          fork test, or(is-above(d-lo, 0.0), is-below(d-hi, 0.0))
            hold
              save m, subtract(greater(absolute-of(d-lo), absolute-of(d-hi)), 1.0)
              sift a
                case no-value
                  back make no-value
                case within
                  link n-lo
                  link n-hi
                  fork test, is-minimum(n-lo, 0.0)
                    hold
                      back make-span(0.0, lesser(n-hi, m))
                  fork test, is-maximum(n-hi, 0.0)
                    hold
                      back make-span(greater(n-lo, subtract(0.0, m)), 0.0)
                  back make-span(subtract(0.0, m), m)
                case any-value
                  back make-span(subtract(0.0, m), m)
        miss
          save idle, 0

  sift a
    case no-value
      back make no-value
    case any-value
      sift b
        case no-value
          back make no-value
        miss
          back make any-value
    case within
      link a-lo
      link a-hi
      sift b
        case no-value
          back make no-value
        case any-value
          back make any-value
        case within
          link b-lo
          link b-hi
          fork test, is-equal(op, <+>)
            hold
              back make-span(add(a-lo, b-lo), add(a-hi, b-hi))
          fork test, is-equal(op, <->)
            hold
              back make-span(subtract(a-lo, b-hi), subtract(a-hi, b-lo))
          fork test, is-equal(op, <*>)
            hold
              save c1, times(a-lo, b-lo)
              save c2, times(a-lo, b-hi)
              save c3, times(a-hi, b-lo)
              save c4, times(a-hi, b-hi)
              back make-span(lesser(lesser(c1, c2), lesser(c3, c4)), greater(greater(c1, c2), greater(c3, c4)))
          # an integer quotient is no larger than its dividend, and not negative when both sides are not; a zero
          # divisor stops the program
          fork test, is-equal(op, </>)
            hold
              fork test, and(is-maximum(b-lo, 0.0), is-minimum(b-hi, 0.0))
                hold
                  back make any-value
              fork test, and(is-minimum(a-lo, 0.0), is-above(b-lo, 0.0))
                hold
                  back make-span(0.0, a-hi)
              save m, greater(absolute-of(a-lo), absolute-of(a-hi))
              back make-span(subtract(0.0, m), m)
          back make any-value

# a value narrowed by one fact against its bound's interval, no value where nothing is left
task narrow-by
  take v, like span-value
  take op, like text
  take bound, like span-value
  like span-value
  mark private

  sift v
    case no-value
      back v
    miss
      save idle, 0
  save b-lo, 0.0
  save b-hi, 0.0
  sift bound
    case within
      link given-lo
      link given-hi
      save b-lo, given-lo
      save b-hi, given-hi
    miss
      back v
  save lo, minus-infinity()
  save hi, infinity()
  sift v
    case within
      link v-lo
      link v-hi
      save lo, v-lo
      save hi, v-hi
    miss
      save idle, 0

  fork test, is-equal(op, <\<>)
    hold
      save hi, lesser(hi, subtract(b-hi, 1.0))
  fork test, is-equal(op, <\<=>)
    hold
      save hi, lesser(hi, b-hi)
  fork test, is-equal(op, <\>>)
    hold
      save lo, greater(lo, add(b-lo, 1.0))
  fork test, is-equal(op, <\>=>)
    hold
      save lo, greater(lo, b-lo)
  fork test, is-equal(op, <==>)
    hold
      save lo, greater(lo, b-lo)
      save hi, lesser(hi, b-hi)
  # only a single excluded value at an end moves it
  fork test, is-equal(op, <!=>)
    hold
      fork test, and(is-equal(b-lo, b-hi), is-equal(lo, b-lo))
        hold
          save lo, add(lo, 1.0)
        miss
          fork test, and(is-equal(b-lo, b-hi), is-equal(hi, b-hi))
            hold
              save hi, subtract(hi, 1.0)

  fork test, is-above(lo, hi)
    hold
      back make no-value
  back make-span(lo, hi)

# ---- the nodes, by their place ----

# one place in node-reach's order: an expression or a statement
form numbered-node
  case expression-at
    link node, like expression
  case statement-at
    link node, like statement

# a body's nodes by place, and the size of each subtree asked for so far
form numbered
  mark shared
  link nodes, like list, like numbered-node
  link sizes, like hash, like number, like number

task skipped
  like list, like text
  mark private

  save out, make list
  push(out, <type>)
  push(out, <span>)
  back out

task numbered-of
  take statements, like list, like statement
  like numbered
  mark private

  save seen, reach-statements(statements, skipped())
  save nodes, make list
  save e, 0
  save s, 0
  walk seen/order
    take is-expression
    fork test, is-expression
      hold
        save one
          make expression-at
            bind node, get(seen/expressions, e)
        push(nodes, one)
        save e, add(e, 1)
      miss
        save one
          make statement-at
            bind node, get(seen/statements, s)
        push(nodes, one)
        save s, add(s, 1)
  back
    make numbered
      bind nodes, nodes
      bind sizes, make hash

# how many places the subtree at `at` holds, itself included: node-reach's own count of it
task extent
  take nb, like numbered
  take at, like number
  like number
  mark private

  fork test, nb/sizes/has(at)
    hold
      back nb/sizes/get(at)
  save size, 0
  sift get(nb/nodes, at)
    case expression-at
      link node
      save size, reach-expression(node, skipped())/order/length
    case statement-at
      link node
      save one, make list
      push(one, node)
      save size, reach-statements(one, skipped())/order/length
  save nb/sizes/{at}, size
  back size

# the places a block's statements take, from `start`
task block-size
  take nb, like numbered
  take body, like list, like statement
  take start, like number
  like number
  mark private

  save at, start
  walk body
    take one
    save at, add(at, extent(nb, at))
  back subtract(at, start)

# ---- reading nodes ----

task kind-of
  take given, like maybe, like type
  like text
  mark private

  sift given
    case some
      link known
      back known/kind
    case none
      back <>

task is-number
  take e, like expression
  like boolean
  mark private

  back is-equal(kind-of(expression-type(e)), <number>)

task binding-kind
  take given, like maybe, like binding
  like text
  mark private

  sift given
    case some
      link bound
      back bound/kind
    case none
      back <>

task variable-name
  take e, like expression
  like text
  mark private

  sift e
    case variable
      link name
      back name
    miss
      back <>

task is-variable
  take e, like expression
  like boolean
  mark private

  sift e
    case variable
      back true
    miss
      back false

# the original's `/^\d+$/`: one or more ASCII digits and nothing else
task is-digits
  take value, like text
  like boolean
  mark private

  fork test, is-equal(value, <>)
    hold
      back false
  walk split(value, <>)
    take char
    fork test, not(contains(split(<0123456789>, <>), char))
      hold
        back false
  back true

# a slot read or written by index: `xs/{i}` or a literal `xs/0`
task is-slot
  take e, like expression
  like boolean
  mark private

  sift e
    case member
      link target
      link field-name
      link slot-index
      sift slot-index
        case some
          back true
        case none
          back is-digits(field-name)
    miss
      back false

# the named type an expression has, or empty
task named-type
  take e, like expression
  like text
  mark private

  sift expression-type(e)
    case some
      link known
      sift known
        case named
          link type-name
          back type-name
        miss
          back <>
    case none
      back <>

task is-none-method
  take given, like maybe, like method-of
  like boolean
  mark private

  sift given
    case some
      back false
    case none
      back true

task slot-target
  take e, like expression
  like expression
  mark private

  sift e
    case member
      link target
      back target
    miss
      back e

# ---- the program, and the context of one walk ----

# what stops a loop, collected while its body runs
form loop-exits
  mark shared
  link breaks, like list, like maybe, like hash, like text, like span-value
  link continues, like list, like maybe, like hash, like text, like span-value

form loop-result
  link head, like maybe, like hash, like text, like span-value
  link breaks, like list, like maybe, like hash, like text, like span-value

# one task: what the static scan found, by place, and each place's identity: the node object it holds, numbered by
# the face across every task, so a node the program shares between places is one node here as it was there
form walked-task
  mark shared
  link name, like text
  link params, like list, like text
  link body, like list, like statement
  link nb, like numbered
  link ids, like list, like number
  link excluded, like hash, like text, like boolean
  link stable, like hash, like text, like boolean
  link reads, like hash, like text, like boolean
  link spent, like boolean

form walk-context
  mark shared
  link owned, like hash, like text, like boolean
  link lend, like hash, like text, like hash, like number, like text
  link plain, like hash, like text, like boolean
  link number-fields, like hash, like text, like list, like text
  link closed, like hash, like text, like boolean
  link answers, like hash, like text, like boolean
  link closure-writes, like hash, like text, like boolean
  link unknown-keys, like hash, like text, like boolean
  link arities, like hash, like text, like list, like number
  link walkers, like boolean
  # what each node gives a global when it is evaluated, and what it evaluated to, joined over every walk: by identity
  link contrib, like hash, like number, like list, like text
  link recorded, like hash, like number, like span-value
  link globals, like hash, like text, like span-value
  link found, like hash, like text, like span-value
  link reading, like hash, like text, like boolean
  link steps, like number
  link spent, like boolean
  link in-closure, like boolean
  link loops, like list, like loop-exits

# the owned key a path `r/field` names
task path-key
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take e, like expression
  like maybe, like text
  mark private

  sift e
    case member
      link target
      link field-name
      link slot-index
      sift slot-index
        case some
          back make none
        case none
          save type-name, named-type(target)
          fork test, and(is-unequal(type-name, <>), ctx/plain/has(type-name))
            hold
              save key, <{type-name}/{field-name}>
              fork test, ctx/owned/has(key)
                hold
                  back make(some, key)
          back make none
    miss
      back make none

# the field key a path `r.field` names, when it reads a plain record's number field
task field-key
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take e, like expression
  like maybe, like text
  mark private

  sift e
    case member
      link target
      link field-name
      link slot-index
      sift slot-index
        case some
          back make none
        case none
          fork test, is-digits(field-name)
            hold
              back make none
          save type-name, named-type(target)
          fork test, and(is-unequal(type-name, <>), ctx/number-fields/has(type-name))
            hold
              fork test, contains(ctx/number-fields/get(type-name), field-name)
                hold
                  save key, <{type-name}.{field-name}>
                  back make(some, key)
          back make none
    miss
      back make none

# the key a written or read path names: an owned slot, or a number field
task path-or-field
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take e, like expression
  like maybe, like text
  mark private

  fork test, is-slot(e)
    hold
      back path-key(ctx, slot-target(e))
  back field-key(ctx, e)

task give
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take one, like walked-task
  take at, like number
  take key, like text
  like void
  mark private

  save id, get(one/ids, at)
  fork test, ctx/contrib/has(id)
    hold
      push(ctx/contrib/get(id), key)
    miss
      save fresh, make list
      push(fresh, key)
      save ctx/contrib/{id}, fresh

task read-global
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take key, like text
  like span-value
  mark private

  save ctx/reading/{key}, true
  back ctx/globals/get(key)

task put
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take key, like text
  take v, like span-value
  like void
  mark private

  fork test, and(ctx/globals/has(key), not(is-no-value(v)))
    hold
      save before, ctx/found/get-or-default(key, nothing())
      save ctx/found/{key}, join-values(before, v)

# ---- the static scan ----

task function-name
  take one, like statement
  like text
  mark private

  sift one
    case function
      link name
      back name
    miss
      back <>

task function-params
  take one, like statement
  like list, like text
  mark private

  save out, make list
  sift one
    case function
      link params
      walk params
        take param
        push(out, param/name)
    miss
      save idle, 0
  back out

task function-body
  take one, like statement
  like list, like statement
  mark private

  sift one
    case function
      link body
      back body
    miss
      back make list

# the places of a list of expressions held one after another from `start`
task places-of
  take nb, like numbered
  take values, like list, like expression
  take start, like number
  like list, like number
  mark private

  save out, make list
  save at, start
  walk values
    take value
    take i
    push(out, at)
    fork test, is-below(add(i, 1), values/length)
      hold
        save at, add(at, extent(nb, at))
  back out

task scan-statement
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take one, like walked-task
  take s, like statement
  take at, like number
  take declared, like hash, like text, like number
  take assigned, like hash, like text, like boolean
  like void
  mark private

  sift s
    case let
      link name
      save declared/{name}, add(declared/get-or-default(name, 0), 1)
    case assign
      link target
      link assign-op
      link given
      link assign-span
      sift target
        case variable
          link target-name
          save assigned/{target-name}, true
        miss
          save idle, 0
      # a slot written through an owned path, and a number field written through a path
      sift path-or-field(ctx, target)
        case some
          link key
          fork test, is-equal(to-text(assign-op), <=>)
            hold
              give(ctx, one,add(add(at, 1), extent(one/nb, add(at, 1))), key)
            miss
              save ctx/unknown-keys/{key}, true
        case none
          save idle, 0
    case for-each
      link item
      link index
      save one/excluded/{item}, true
      fork test, is-unequal(index, <>)
        hold
          save one/excluded/{index}, true
    case match
      link cases
      walk cases
        take arm
        walk arm/binds
          take bound
          save one/excluded/{bound}, true
    case guard
      link body
      link handler
      sift handler
        case some
          link clause
          fork test, is-unequal(clause/name, <>)
            hold
              save one/excluded/{clause/name}, true
        case none
          save idle, 0
    miss
      save idle, 0

task scan-expression
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take one, like walked-task
  take e, like expression
  take at, like number
  take stored, like hash, like text, like text
  like void
  mark private

  sift e
    case variable
      link name
      link binding
      # a name the task reads as something other than a local or a parameter
      save kind, binding-kind(binding)
      fork test, and(is-unequal(kind, <>), and(is-unequal(kind, <local>), is-unequal(kind, <parameter>)))
        hold
          save one/excluded/{name}, true
    case call
      link callee
      link args
      save callee-name, variable-name(callee)
      fork test, ctx/closed/has(callee-name)
        hold
          fork test, ctx/arities/has(callee-name)
            hold
              push(ctx/arities/get(callee-name), args/length)
            miss
              save counts, make list
              push(counts, args/length)
              save ctx/arities/{callee-name}, counts
          save places, places-of(one/nb, args, add(add(at, 1), extent(one/nb, add(at, 1))))
          walk places
            take place
            take i
            give(ctx, one,place, <param:{callee-name}:{i}>)
      # the form walkers build any record, with any field
      fork test, or(is-equal(callee-name, <fill-form>), is-equal(callee-name, <melt-form>))
        hold
          save ctx/walkers, true
    case closure
      link params
      walk params
        take param
        save one/excluded/{param/name}, true
    case record
      link name
      link fields
      link positional
      save record-name, name
      save places, make list
      fork test, is-above(fields/length, 0)
        hold
          save values, make list
          walk fields
            take field
            push(values, field/value)
          save places, places-of(one/nb, values, add(at, 1))
      # a construction: an owned field given an empty list adds nothing, a local adds what that local was given,
      # anything else is unknown
      fork test, ctx/plain/has(record-name)
        hold
          walk fields
            take field
            save key, <{record-name}/{field/name}>
            save skip, not(ctx/owned/has(key))
            sift field/value
              case array
                link items
                fork test, is-equal(items/length, 0)
                  hold
                    save skip, true
              miss
                save idle, 0
            fork test, not(skip)
              hold
                sift field/value
                  case variable
                    link local
                    save stored/{local}, key
                  miss
                    save ctx/unknown-keys/{key}, true
      # each number field given its value, or unknown when the construction leaves it out or fills by position
      fork test, ctx/number-fields/has(record-name)
        hold
          walk ctx/number-fields/get(record-name)
            take number-field
            save key, <{record-name}.{number-field}>
            save given-at, -1
            walk fields
              take field
              take i
              fork test, is-equal(field/name, number-field)
                hold
                  save given-at, get(places, i)
                  halt
            fork test, and(is-minimum(given-at, 0), is-equal(positional/length, 0))
              hold
                give(ctx, one,given-at, key)
              miss
                save ctx/unknown-keys/{key}, true
    miss
      save idle, 0

# What a local list is given in a body: each literal item of its `let`, each value pushed onto it, each value written
# into one of its slots. Unknown when anything else could put a value in: a `let` from anything but a list literal or an
# empty list, a compound write into a slot, the local passed to a task that writes it, or the local written whole
task elements-of
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take one, like walked-task
  take local, like text
  take key, like text
  like void
  mark private

  save nb, one/nb
  walk nb/nodes
    take node
    take at
    sift node
      case statement-at
        link s
        sift s
          case let
            link name
            link init
            fork test, is-equal(name, local)
              hold
                sift init
                  case array
                    link items
                    walk places-of(nb, items, add(at, 2))
                      take place
                      give(ctx, one,place, key)
                  case record
                    link record-name
                    link fields
                    fork test, not(and(is-equal(record-name, <list>), is-equal(fields/length, 0)))
                      hold
                        save ctx/unknown-keys/{key}, true
                  miss
                    save ctx/unknown-keys/{key}, true
          case assign
            link target
            link assign-op
            link given
            fork test, is-equal(variable-name(target), local)
              hold
                save ctx/unknown-keys/{key}, true
            fork test, and(is-slot(target), is-equal(variable-name(slot-target(target)), local))
              hold
                fork test, is-equal(to-text(assign-op), <=>)
                  hold
                    give(ctx, one,add(add(at, 1), extent(nb, add(at, 1))), key)
                  miss
                    save ctx/unknown-keys/{key}, true
          miss
            save idle, 0
      case expression-at
        link e
        sift e
          case call
            link callee
            link args
            save callee-name, variable-name(callee)
            save places, places-of(nb, args, add(add(at, 1), extent(nb, add(at, 1))))
            walk args
              take arg
              take i
              fork test, is-equal(variable-name(arg), local)
                hold
                  fork test, and(is-equal(callee-name, <list_push>), is-equal(i, 0))
                    hold
                      fork test, is-above(args/length, 1)
                        hold
                          give(ctx, one,get(places, 1), key)
                    miss
                      fork test, and(contains(list-length-tasks(), callee-name), is-equal(i, 0))
                        hold
                          # its size, read
                          save idle, 0
                        miss
                          fork test, not(lent-read(ctx, callee-name, i))
                            hold
                              save ctx/unknown-keys/{key}, true
            # a push through the collection operation, `xs.push(v)`
            sift callee
              case member
                link target
                link field-name
                fork test, and(is-equal(field-name, <push>), is-equal(variable-name(target), local))
                  hold
                    walk places
                      take place
                      give(ctx, one,place, key)
              miss
                save idle, 0
          miss
            save idle, 0

# whether a task takes its list parameter `at` lent for reading
task lent-read
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take name, like text
  take at, like number
  like boolean
  mark private

  fork test, or(is-equal(name, <>), not(ctx/lend/has(name)))
    hold
      back false
  save by-place, ctx/lend/get(name)
  fork test, by-place/has(at)
    hold
      back is-equal(by-place/get(at), <read>)
  back false

task scan-task
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take fn, like statement
  take ids, like list, like number
  like walked-task
  mark private

  save params, function-params(fn)
  save body, function-body(fn)
  save one
    make walked-task
      bind name, function-name(fn)
      bind params, params
      bind body, body
      bind nb, numbered-of(body)
      bind ids, ids
      bind excluded, make hash
      bind stable, make hash
      bind reads, make hash
      bind spent, false
  save declared, make hash
  walk params
    take param
    save declared/{param}, 1
  save assigned, make hash
  # the stored locals of this task: a construction handing one into an owned field
  save stored, make hash
  walk one/nb/nodes
    take node
    take at
    sift node
      case statement-at
        link s
        scan-statement(ctx, one, s, at, declared, assigned)
      case expression-at
        link e
        scan-expression(ctx, one, e, at, stored)

  walk ctx/closure-writes/keys()
    take written
    save one/excluded/{written}, true

  walk stored/keys()
    take local
    elements-of(ctx, one, local, stored/get(local))

  walk declared/keys()
    take name
    fork test, and(is-equal(declared/get(name), 1), and(not(assigned/has(name)), not(one/excluded/has(name))))
      hold
        save one/stable/{name}, true
  back one

# every variable name an assignment inside some closure writes
task names-written-in-closures
  take nb, like numbered
  like hash, like text, like boolean
  mark private

  save names, make hash
  save inside-until, -1
  walk nb/nodes
    take node
    take at
    sift node
      case expression-at
        link e
        sift e
          case closure
            save end, add(at, extent(nb, at))
            fork test, is-above(end, inside-until)
              hold
                save inside-until, end
          miss
            save idle, 0
      case statement-at
        link s
        fork test, is-below(at, inside-until)
          hold
            sift s
              case assign
                link target
                save written, variable-name(target)
                fork test, is-unequal(written, <>)
                  hold
                    save names/{written}, true
              miss
                save idle, 0
  back names

# every name read as a value other than a local or a parameter, and not as a call's callee
task names-referenced
  take nb, like numbered
  like hash, like text, like boolean
  mark private

  save named, make hash
  save callees, make hash
  walk nb/nodes
    take node
    take at
    sift node
      case expression-at
        link e
        sift e
          case call
            save callees/{add(at, 1)}, true
          case variable
            link name
            link binding
            save kind, binding-kind(binding)
            fork test, and(not(callees/has(at)), and(is-unequal(kind, <local>), is-unequal(kind, <parameter>)))
              hold
                save named/{name}, true
          miss
            save idle, 0
      case statement-at
        save idle, 0
  back named

# ---- the walk of one task ----

task count-step
  take ctx, like walk-context
  like void
  mark private

  save ctx/steps, add(ctx/steps, 1)
  fork test, is-above(ctx/steps, step-budget())
    hold
      save ctx/spent, true

task copy-names
  take vars, like hash, like text, like span-value
  like hash, like text, like span-value
  mark private

  save out, make hash
  walk vars/keys()
    take name
    save out/{name}, vars/get(name)
  back out

task copy-state
  take state, like maybe, like hash, like text, like span-value
  like maybe, like hash, like text, like span-value
  mark private

  sift state
    case some
      link vars
      save copied, copy-names(vars)
      back make(some, copied)
    case none
      back make none

# a name written into a state, unless the task never tracks it
task set-name
  take one, like walked-task
  take vars, like hash, like text, like span-value
  take name, like text
  take v, like span-value
  like void
  mark private

  fork test, not(one/excluded/has(name))
    hold
      save vars/{name}, v

task join-states
  take states, like list, like maybe, like hash, like text, like span-value
  like maybe, like hash, like text, like span-value
  mark private

  save live, make list
  walk states
    take state
    sift state
      case some
        link vars
        push(live, vars)
      case none
        save idle, 0
  fork test, is-equal(live/length, 0)
    hold
      back make none
  fork test, is-equal(live/length, 1)
    hold
      save only, get(live, 0)
      back make(some, only)
  save out, make hash
  walk live
    take vars
    walk vars/keys()
      take name
      fork test, out/has(name)
        hold
          save out/{name}, join-values(out/get(name), vars/get(name))
        miss
          save out/{name}, vars/get(name)
  back make(some, out)

task same-states
  take a, like maybe, like hash, like text, like span-value
  take b, like maybe, like hash, like text, like span-value
  like boolean
  mark private

  sift a
    case none
      sift b
        case none
          back true
        case some
          back false
    case some
      link a-vars
      sift b
        case none
          back false
        case some
          link b-vars
          save a-names, a-vars/keys()
          fork test, is-unequal(a-names/length, b-vars/keys()/length)
            hold
              back false
          walk a-names
            take name
            fork test, not(b-vars/has(name))
              hold
                back false
            fork test, not(same-values(a-vars/get(name), b-vars/get(name)))
              hold
                back false
          back true

task widen-states
  take before, like maybe, like hash, like text, like span-value
  take after, like maybe, like hash, like text, like span-value
  like maybe, like hash, like text, like span-value
  mark private

  sift before
    case some
      link before-vars
      sift after
        case some
          link after-vars
          save out, make hash
          walk after-vars/keys()
            take name
            fork test, before-vars/has(name)
              hold
                save out/{name}, widen(before-vars/get(name), after-vars/get(name))
              miss
                save out/{name}, after-vars/get(name)
          back make(some, out)
        case none
          back after
    case none
      back after

# what a condition says when it is `truth`: `name op bound`, from a comparison with a name on either side, both sides of
# an `&&` that held or an `||` that failed, and a `!` turned over. Anything else says nothing, which is only less precise
form fact
  link name, like text
  link op, like text
  link bound, like expression
  link at, like number

task is-comparison
  take op, like text
  like boolean
  mark private

  back or(or(or(is-equal(op, <\<>), is-equal(op, <\<=>)), or(is-equal(op, <\>>), is-equal(op, <\>=>))), or(is-equal(op, <==>), is-equal(op, <!=>)))

task negate-op
  take op, like text
  like text
  mark private

  fork test, is-equal(op, <\<>)
    hold
      back <\>=>
  fork test, is-equal(op, <\<=>)
    hold
      back <\>>
  fork test, is-equal(op, <\>>)
    hold
      back <\<=>
  fork test, is-equal(op, <\>=>)
    hold
      back <\<>
  fork test, is-equal(op, <==>)
    hold
      back <!=>
  back <==>

task flip-op
  take op, like text
  like text
  mark private

  fork test, is-equal(op, <\<>)
    hold
      back <\>>
  fork test, is-equal(op, <\<=>)
    hold
      back <\>=>
  fork test, is-equal(op, <\>>)
    hold
      back <\<>
  fork test, is-equal(op, <\>=>)
    hold
      back <\<=>
  back op

task condition-facts
  take one, like walked-task
  take cond, like expression
  take at, like number
  take truth, like boolean
  like list, like fact
  mark private

  sift cond
    case unary
      link un-op
      link operand
      fork test, is-equal(to-text(un-op), <!>)
        hold
          back condition-facts(one, operand, add(at, 1), not(truth))
      back make list
    case binary
      link bin-op
      link left
      link right
      save op, to-text(bin-op)
      save right-at, add(add(at, 1), extent(one/nb, add(at, 1)))
      fork test, or(and(is-equal(op, <&&>), truth), and(is-equal(op, <||>), not(truth)))
        hold
          save both, condition-facts(one, left, add(at, 1), truth)
          walk condition-facts(one, right, right-at, truth)
            take f
            push(both, f)
          back both
      fork test, or(not(is-comparison(op)), or(not(is-number(left)), not(is-number(right))))
        hold
          back make list
      save held, op
      fork test, not(truth)
        hold
          save held, negate-op(op)
      save facts, make list
      save left-name, variable-name(left)
      fork test, is-variable(left)
        hold
          save on-left
            make fact
              bind name, left-name
              bind op, held
              bind bound, right
              bind at, right-at
          push(facts, on-left)
      save right-name, variable-name(right)
      fork test, is-variable(right)
        hold
          save on-right
            make fact
              bind name, right-name
              bind op, flip-op(held)
              bind bound, left
              bind at, add(at, 1)
          push(facts, on-right)
      back facts
    miss
      back make list

# a condition's facts applied to a state, no state where the condition cannot be `truth` there
task refine
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take one, like walked-task
  take state, like maybe, like hash, like text, like span-value
  take cond, like expression
  take at, like number
  take truth, like boolean
  like maybe, like hash, like text, like span-value
  mark private

  sift state
    case none
      back make none
    case some
      link vars
      # always a new state, so the caller may change it
      save out, copy-names(vars)
      walk condition-facts(one, cond, at, truth)
        take f
        fork test, out/has(f/name)
          hold
            save current, out/get(f/name)
            save narrowed, narrow-by(current, f/op, evaluate(ctx, one, f/bound, f/at, state, true))
            fork test, is-no-value(narrowed)
              hold
                back make none
            set-name(one, out, f/name, narrowed)
      back make(some, out)

# an expression's value in a state. `quiet` reads without recording or giving, for a condition's bound
task evaluate
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take one, like walked-task
  take e, like expression
  take at, like number
  take state, like maybe, like hash, like text, like span-value
  take quiet, like boolean
  like span-value
  mark private

  fork test, ctx/spent
    hold
      back make any-value
  sift state
    case none
      back make no-value
    case some
      link vars
      back evaluate-live(ctx, one, e, at, vars, quiet)

task evaluate-maybe
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take one, like walked-task
  take given, like maybe, like expression
  take at, like number
  take state, like maybe, like hash, like text, like span-value
  take quiet, like boolean
  like span-value
  mark private

  sift given
    case some
      link e
      back evaluate(ctx, one, e, at, state, quiet)
    case none
      back make no-value

task evaluate-each
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take one, like walked-task
  take values, like list, like expression
  take start, like number
  take state, like maybe, like hash, like text, like span-value
  take quiet, like boolean
  like void
  mark private

  save at, start
  walk values
    take value
    take i
    evaluate(ctx, one, value, at, state, quiet)
    fork test, is-below(add(i, 1), values/length)
      hold
        save at, add(at, extent(one/nb, at))

task evaluate-live
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take one, like walked-task
  take e, like expression
  take at, like number
  take vars, like hash, like text, like span-value
  take quiet, like boolean
  like span-value
  mark private

  count-step(ctx)
  fork test, ctx/spent
    hold
      back make any-value
  save state, make(some, vars)
  save v, make any-value
  save first, add(at, 1)

  sift e
    case integer
      link given
      save n, to-decimal(given)
      save v, make-span(n, n)
    case variable
      link name
      fork test, vars/has(name)
        hold
          save v, vars/get(name)
    case unary
      link un-op
      link operand
      save inner, evaluate(ctx, one, operand, first, state, quiet)
      fork test, and(is-equal(to-text(un-op), <->), is-number(operand))
        hold
          sift inner
            case within
              link in-lo
              link in-hi
              save v, make-span(subtract(0.0, in-hi), subtract(0.0, in-lo))
            miss
              save v, inner
    case binary
      link bin-op
      link left
      link right
      save op, to-text(bin-op)
      save a, evaluate(ctx, one, left, first, state, quiet)
      # the right side of `&&` and `||` runs only where the left allowed it
      save right-state, state
      fork test, is-equal(op, <&&>)
        hold
          save right-state, refine(ctx, one, state, left, first, true)
      fork test, is-equal(op, <||>)
        hold
          save right-state, refine(ctx, one, state, left, first, false)
      save b, evaluate(ctx, one, right, add(first, extent(one/nb, first)), right-state, quiet)
      fork test, and(or(or(or(is-equal(op, <+>), is-equal(op, <->)), or(is-equal(op, <*>), is-equal(op, </>))), is-equal(op, <%>)), and(is-number(left), is-number(right)))
        hold
          save v, arith(op, a, b)
    case member
      link target
      link field-name
      link slot-index
      evaluate(ctx, one, target, first, state, quiet)
      evaluate-maybe(ctx, one, slot-index, add(first, extent(one/nb, first)), state, quiet)
      sift path-or-field(ctx, e)
        case some
          link key
          save v, read-global(ctx, key)
        case none
          save idle, 0
    case call
      link callee
      link args
      fork test, not(is-variable(callee))
        hold
          evaluate(ctx, one, callee, first, state, quiet)
      evaluate-each(ctx, one, args, add(first, extent(one/nb, first)), state, quiet)
      sift callee
        case variable
          link name
          link binding
          fork test, and(ctx/answers/has(name), is-equal(binding-kind(binding), <function>))
            hold
              save v, read-global(ctx, <task:{name}>)
        miss
          save idle, 0
    case conditional
      link branches
      link otherwise
      save rest, state
      save v, make no-value
      save q, first
      walk branches
        take branch
        evaluate(ctx, one, branch/cond, q, rest, quiet)
        save value-at, add(q, extent(one/nb, q))
        save taken, refine(ctx, one, rest, branch/cond, q, true)
        save v, join-values(v, evaluate(ctx, one, branch/value, value-at, taken, quiet))
        save rest, refine(ctx, one, rest, branch/cond, q, false)
        save q, add(value-at, extent(one/nb, value-at))
      save v, join-values(v, evaluate-maybe(ctx, one, otherwise, q, rest, quiet))
    case closure
      link body
      fork test, not(quiet)
        hold
          run-closure(ctx, one, body, first, vars)
    case array
      link items
      evaluate-each(ctx, one, items, first, state, quiet)
    case map
      link entries
      save q, first
      walk entries
        take entry
        evaluate(ctx, one, entry/key, q, state, quiet)
        save value-at, add(q, extent(one/nb, q))
        evaluate(ctx, one, entry/value, value-at, state, quiet)
        save q, add(value-at, extent(one/nb, value-at))
    case record
      link fields
      link positional
      save values, make list
      walk fields
        take field
        push(values, field/value)
      evaluate-each(ctx, one, values, first, state, quiet)
      # a `need false` list, walked where it is read so nothing is written into the program
      fork test, is-above(positional/length, 0)
        hold
          save q, add(first, block-places(one/nb, values, first))
          walk positional
            take one-positional
            evaluate(ctx, one, one-positional, q, state, quiet)
            save q, add(q, extent(one/nb, q))
    case template
      link parts
      save values, make list
      walk parts
        take part
        sift part
          case value
            link inner
            push(values, inner)
          case chunk
            save idle, 0
      evaluate-each(ctx, one, values, first, state, quiet)
    case await
      link expr
      evaluate(ctx, one, expr, first, state, quiet)
    miss
      save idle, 0

  fork test, and(not(quiet), and(not(is-no-value(v)), not(ctx/spent)))
    hold
      save id, get(one/ids, at)
      save before, ctx/recorded/get-or-default(id, nothing())
      save ctx/recorded/{id}, join-values(before, v)
      fork test, ctx/contrib/has(id)
        hold
          walk ctx/contrib/get(id)
            take key
            put(ctx, key, v)
  back v

# the places a list of expressions takes, from `start`
task block-places
  take nb, like numbered
  take values, like list, like expression
  take start, like number
  like number
  mark private

  save at, start
  walk values
    take value
    save at, add(at, extent(nb, at))
  back subtract(at, start)

# a closure's body, run where it is made: it may run then or at any later time, so it sees only the names that never
# change
task run-closure
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take one, like walked-task
  take body, like list, like statement
  take start, like number
  take vars, like hash, like text, like span-value
  like void
  mark private

  save entry, make hash
  walk vars/keys()
    take name
    fork test, one/stable/has(name)
      hold
        save entry/{name}, vars/get(name)
  save outer-loops, ctx/loops
  save ctx/loops, make list
  save outer, ctx/in-closure
  save ctx/in-closure, true
  run(ctx, one, body, start, make(some, entry))
  save ctx/in-closure, outer
  save ctx/loops, outer-loops

task run
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take one, like walked-task
  take body, like list, like statement
  take start, like number
  take state, like maybe, like hash, like text, like span-value
  like maybe, like hash, like text, like span-value
  mark private

  save s, state
  save at, start
  walk body
    take statement
    take i
    sift s
      case none
        back make none
      case some
        link vars
        save s, run-statement(ctx, one, statement, at, vars)
    fork test, is-below(add(i, 1), body/length)
      hold
        save at, add(at, extent(one/nb, at))
  back s

task new-exits
  like loop-exits
  mark private

  back
    make loop-exits
      bind breaks, make list
      bind continues, make list

task drop-last-loop
  take ctx, like walk-context
  like void
  mark private

  save kept, make list
  walk ctx/loops
    take loop
    take i
    fork test, is-below(add(i, 1), ctx/loops/length)
      hold
        push(kept, loop)
  save ctx/loops, kept

# a turn's way in: the condition evaluated and taken true, for a `while`, or the head as it is
task enter
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take one, like walked-task
  take head, like maybe, like hash, like text, like span-value
  take cond, like maybe, like expression
  take at, like number
  like maybe, like hash, like text, like span-value
  mark private

  sift cond
    case some
      link test-expr
      evaluate(ctx, one, test-expr, at, head, false)
      back refine(ctx, one, head, test-expr, at, true)
    case none
      back head

# a loop body iterated to a fixpoint from `entry`, each turn entered through `enter`, widened after a few turns, then
# narrowed once: the state at the loop's head and the breaks
task iterate
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take one, like walked-task
  take entry, like hash, like text, like span-value
  take cond, like maybe, like expression
  take cond-at, like number
  take body, like list, like statement
  take body-at, like number
  like loop-result
  mark private

  save head, make(some, entry)
  save breaks, make list
  save turn, 0
  walk test
    hook test, true
    hook hold
      save exits, new-exits()
      push(ctx/loops, exits)
      save out, run(ctx, one, body, body-at, copy-state(enter(ctx, one, head, cond, cond-at)))
      drop-last-loop(ctx)
      save breaks, exits/breaks
      save joined, make list
      push(joined, head)
      push(joined, out)
      walk exits/continues
        take c
        push(joined, c)
      save next, join-states(joined)
      fork test, same-states(next, head)
        hold
          halt
      fork test, is-minimum(turn, widen-turns())
        hold
          save head, widen-states(head, next)
        miss
          save head, next
      save turn, add(turn, 1)
      fork test, ctx/spent
        hold
          halt

  # one narrowing turn from the fixpoint: the entry joined with what a turn gives back
  save exits, new-exits()
  push(ctx/loops, exits)
  save out, run(ctx, one, body, body-at, copy-state(enter(ctx, one, head, cond, cond-at)))
  drop-last-loop(ctx)
  save joined, make list
  push(joined, make(some, entry))
  push(joined, out)
  walk exits/continues
    take c
    push(joined, c)
  save all-breaks, make list
  walk breaks
    take b
    push(all-breaks, b)
  walk exits/breaks
    take b
    push(all-breaks, b)
  back
    make loop-result
      bind head, join-states(joined)
      bind breaks, all-breaks

# every name an assignment or a `let` writes among the places from `start` up to `stop`
task assigned-names
  take nb, like numbered
  take start, like number
  take stop, like number
  like list, like text
  mark private

  save out, make list
  save at, start
  walk test
    hook test, is-below(at, stop)
    hook hold
      sift get(nb/nodes, at)
        case statement-at
          link s
          sift s
            case assign
              link target
              sift target
                case variable
                  link name
                  push(out, name)
                miss
                  save idle, 0
            case let
              link name
              push(out, name)
            miss
              save idle, 0
        case expression-at
          save idle, 0
      save at, add(at, 1)
  back out

task last-loop-push
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take state, like maybe, like hash, like text, like span-value
  take breaking, like boolean
  like void
  mark private

  fork test, is-above(ctx/loops/length, 0)
    hold
      save loop, get(ctx/loops, subtract(ctx/loops/length, 1))
      fork test, breaking
        hold
          push(loop/breaks, state)
        miss
          push(loop/continues, state)

task run-statement
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take one, like walked-task
  take s, like statement
  take at, like number
  take vars, like hash, like text, like span-value
  like maybe, like hash, like text, like span-value
  mark private

  count-step(ctx)
  fork test, ctx/spent
    hold
      back make none
  save state, make(some, vars)
  save first, add(at, 1)

  sift s
    case let
      link name
      link init
      save v, evaluate(ctx, one, init, first, state, false)
      set-name(one, vars, name, v)
      back state
    case assign
      link target
      link assign-op
      link given
      link assign-span
      save v, evaluate(ctx, one, given, add(first, extent(one/nb, first)), state, false)
      sift target
        case variable
          link target-name
          save op, to-text(assign-op)
          fork test, is-equal(op, <=>)
            hold
              set-name(one, vars, target-name, v)
              back state
          # a compound write is the operation on the name's value
          save current, make any-value
          fork test, vars/has(target-name)
            hold
              save current, vars/get(target-name)
          save next, make any-value
          fork test, and(is-number(target), or(or(is-equal(op, <+=>), is-equal(op, <-=>)), is-equal(op, <*=>)))
            hold
              save next, arith(substring(op, 0, 1), current, v)
          set-name(one, vars, target-name, next)
          back state
        miss
          evaluate(ctx, one, target, first, state, false)
          back state
    case expression
      link expr
      evaluate(ctx, one, expr, first, state, false)
      back state
    case return
      link given
      save v, evaluate-maybe(ctx, one, given, first, state, false)
      sift given
        case some
          fork test, and(not(ctx/in-closure), ctx/answers/has(one/name))
            hold
              put(ctx, <task:{one/name}>, v)
        case none
          save idle, 0
      back make none
    case throw
      link given
      evaluate(ctx, one, given, first, state, false)
      back make none
    case exit
      back make none
    case break
      last-loop-push(ctx, state, true)
      back make none
    case continue
      last-loop-push(ctx, state, false)
      back make none
    case if
      link branches
      link otherwise
      save rest, state
      save outs, make list
      save q, first
      walk branches
        take branch
        evaluate(ctx, one, branch/cond, q, rest, false)
        save body-at, add(q, extent(one/nb, q))
        push(outs, run(ctx, one, branch/body, body-at, refine(ctx, one, rest, branch/cond, q, true)))
        save rest, refine(ctx, one, rest, branch/cond, q, false)
        save q, add(body-at, block-size(one/nb, branch/body, body-at))
      sift otherwise
        case some
          link other
          push(outs, run(ctx, one, other, q, rest))
        case none
          push(outs, rest)
      back join-states(outs)
    case while
      link cond
      link body
      save body-at, add(first, extent(one/nb, first))
      save looped, iterate(ctx, one, vars, make(some, cond), first, body, body-at)
      save outs, make list
      push(outs, refine(ctx, one, looped/head, cond, first, false))
      walk looped/breaks
        take b
        push(outs, b)
      back join-states(outs)
    case for-each
      link iterable
      link body
      evaluate(ctx, one, iterable, first, state, false)
      save body-at, add(first, extent(one/nb, first))
      save no-cond, make none
      save looped, iterate(ctx, one, vars, no-cond, first, body, body-at)
      save outs, make list
      push(outs, looped/head)
      walk looped/breaks
        take b
        push(outs, b)
      back join-states(outs)
    case match
      link subject
      link cases
      link otherwise
      link closed
      evaluate(ctx, one, subject, first, state, false)
      save q, add(first, extent(one/nb, first))
      save outs, make list
      walk cases
        take arm
        push(outs, run(ctx, one, arm/body, q, copy-state(state)))
        save q, add(q, block-size(one/nb, arm/body, q))
      sift otherwise
        case some
          link other
          push(outs, run(ctx, one, other, q, copy-state(state)))
        case none
          fork test, not(closed)
            hold
              push(outs, state)
      back join-states(outs)
    case guard
      link body
      link handler
      save done, run(ctx, one, body, first, copy-state(state))
      # the handler may follow any prefix of the body, so whatever the body assigns is unknown there
      save caught, copy-names(vars)
      save body-end, add(first, block-size(one/nb, body, first))
      walk assigned-names(one/nb, first, body-end)
        take written
        set-name(one, caught, written, make any-value)
      save outs, make list
      push(outs, done)
      sift handler
        case some
          link clause
          push(outs, run(ctx, one, clause/body, body-end, make(some, caught)))
        case none
          push(outs, make(some, caught))
      back join-states(outs)
    miss
      back state

# one task's walk
task walk-task
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take one, like walked-task
  like void
  mark private

  save ctx/steps, 0
  save ctx/spent, false
  save ctx/loops, make list
  save ctx/in-closure, false
  save ctx/reading, make hash
  save entry, make hash
  walk one/params
    take param
    take i
    fork test, not(one/excluded/has(param))
      hold
        fork test, ctx/closed/has(one/name)
          hold
            save entry/{param}, read-global(ctx, <param:{one/name}:{i}>)
          miss
            save entry/{param}, make any-value
  run(ctx, one, one/body, 0, make(some, entry))
  # a task that ran out of steps gives unknown to everything it reaches, and is not walked again
  fork test, ctx/spent
    hold
      save one/spent, true
      walk one/ids
        take id
        fork test, ctx/contrib/has(id)
          hold
            walk ctx/contrib/get(id)
              take key
              put(ctx, key, make any-value)
      fork test, ctx/answers/has(one/name)
        hold
          put(ctx, <task:{one/name}>, make any-value)
  save one/reads, ctx/reading

# ---- the program ----

task recorded-at
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take one, like walked-task
  take at, like number
  like span-value
  mark private

  back ctx/recorded/get-or-default(get(one/ids, at), nothing())

# every integer `+`, `-` and `*` of a task whose value at its own place is inside the bound, and every `/` and `%` whose
# divisor excludes zero (and -1, for a quotient of an unknown)
task proven-in
  take ctx, like walk-context
  take one, like walked-task
  take proven, like list, like expression
  like void
  mark private

  walk one/nb/nodes
    take node
    take at
    sift node
      case expression-at
        link e
        sift e
          case binary
            link bin-op
            link left
            link right
            fork test, and(is-number(left), is-number(right))
              hold
                save op, to-text(bin-op)
                fork test, and(or(or(is-equal(op, <+>), is-equal(op, <->)), is-equal(op, <*>)), finite(recorded-at(ctx, one, at)))
                  hold
                    push(proven, e)
                fork test, or(is-equal(op, <%>), is-equal(op, </>))
                  hold
                    save left-at, add(at, 1)
                    save divisor, recorded-at(ctx, one, add(left-at, extent(one/nb, left-at)))
                    save nonzero, false
                    save not-minus-one, false
                    sift divisor
                      case within
                        link d-lo
                        link d-hi
                        save nonzero, or(is-above(d-lo, 0.0), is-below(d-hi, 0.0))
                        save not-minus-one, and(nonzero, or(is-above(d-lo, 0.0), is-below(d-hi, -1.0)))
                      miss
                        save idle, 0
                    fork test, and(nonzero, or(or(is-equal(op, <%>), not-minus-one), finite(recorded-at(ctx, one, left-at))))
                      hold
                        push(proven, e)
          miss
            save idle, 0
      case statement-at
        save idle, 0

task bounded-arithmetic
  take program, like list, like statement
  # the record list fields the record owns, keyed `form/field` (backend-lending `owned-fields`)
  take owned, like hash, like text, like boolean
  # the list parameters each task takes lent, and whether it writes them (`read` or `write`)
  take lend, like hash, like text, like hash, like number, like text
  # the forms whose values cross into native code: a shim may build one with any field
  take native, like hash, like text, like boolean
  # per task, in the program's order, each place's identity: the first place across every task that holds the same
  # node object (the face numbers them, see the header)
  take ids, like list, like list, like number
  like list, like expression

  save fns, make list
  save plain, make hash
  save number-fields, make hash
  walk program
    take statement
    sift statement
      case function
        push(fns, statement)
      case record-type
        link name
        link fields
        link variants
        fork test, is-equal(variants/length, 0)
          hold
            save plain/{name}, true
            save names, make list
            walk fields
              take field
              save field-type, field/type
              save wrapped, make(some, field-type)
              fork test, is-equal(kind-of(wrapped), <number>)
                hold
                  push(names, field/name)
            save number-fields/{name}, names
      miss
        save idle, 0

  save program-nb, numbered-of(program)

  # the tasks whose every call is in the program and seen here, and the tasks whose answer is the hull of their returns
  save defined, make hash
  walk fns
    take fn
    save name, function-name(fn)
    save defined/{name}, add(defined/get-or-default(name, 0), 1)
  save named, names-referenced(program-nb)
  save closed, make hash
  save answers, make hash
  walk fns
    take fn
    sift fn
      case function
        link name
        link params
        link result
        link internal
        link async
        link method
        save once, is-equal(defined/get(name), 1)
        save simple, and(not(async), is-none-method(method))
        fork test, and(and(internal, simple), and(once, and(not(named/has(name)), is-above(params/length, 0))))
          hold
            save closed/{name}, true
        fork test, and(and(once, simple), is-equal(kind-of(result), <number>))
          hold
            save answers/{name}, true
      miss
        save idle, 0

  save ctx
    make walk-context
      bind owned, owned
      bind lend, lend
      bind plain, plain
      bind number-fields, number-fields
      bind closed, closed
      bind answers, answers
      bind closure-writes, names-written-in-closures(program-nb)
      bind unknown-keys, make hash
      bind arities, make hash
      bind walkers, false
      bind contrib, make hash
      bind recorded, make hash
      bind globals, make hash
      bind found, make hash
      bind reading, make hash
      bind steps, 0
      bind spent, false
      bind in-closure, false
      bind loops, make list

  save tasks, make list
  walk fns
    take fn
    take t
    push(tasks, scan-task(ctx, fn, get(ids, t)))

  # the globals: owned list elements, number fields, closed tasks' parameters, answers
  walk owned/keys()
    take key
    fork test, ctx/unknown-keys/has(key)
      hold
        save ctx/globals/{key}, make any-value
      miss
        save ctx/globals/{key}, make no-value
  walk number-fields/keys()
    take form-name
    walk number-fields/get(form-name)
      take field-name
      save key, <{form-name}.{field-name}>
      fork test, or(or(ctx/walkers, native/has(form-name)), ctx/unknown-keys/has(key))
        hold
          save ctx/globals/{key}, make any-value
        miss
          save ctx/globals/{key}, make no-value
  walk tasks
    take one
    fork test, closed/has(one/name)
      hold
        # a call with another number of arguments leaves the parameters unknown, and a task never called keeps them
        # bottom: its body is never reached
        save bad, false
        walk ctx/arities/get-or-default(one/name, make list)
          take count
          fork test, is-unequal(count, one/params/length)
            hold
              save bad, true
        walk one/params
          take param
          take i
          save key, <param:{one/name}:{i}>
          fork test, bad
            hold
              save ctx/globals/{key}, make any-value
            miss
              save ctx/globals/{key}, make no-value
    fork test, answers/has(one/name)
      hold
        save answer-key, <task:{one/name}>
        save ctx/globals/{answer-key}, make no-value

  save grown, make hash
  save settled, false
  # the tasks a round walks: every one at first, then only those that read a global the last round changed
  save due, tasks
  save round, 0
  walk test
    hook test, is-below(round, 100)
    hook hold
      save ctx/found, make hash
      walk due
        take one
        fork test, not(one/spent)
          hold
            walk-task(ctx, one)
      save changed, make hash
      walk ctx/globals/keys()
        take key
        save before, ctx/globals/get(key)
        save after, join-values(before, ctx/found/get-or-default(key, nothing()))
        fork test, not(same-values(before, after))
          hold
            save times, add(grown/get-or-default(key, 0), 1)
            save grown/{key}, times
            fork test, is-above(times, widen-rounds())
              hold
                save ctx/globals/{key}, widen(before, after)
              miss
                save ctx/globals/{key}, after
            save changed/{key}, true
      fork test, is-equal(changed/keys()/length, 0)
        hold
          save settled, true
          halt
      save next-due, make list
      walk tasks
        take one
        save hit, false
        walk one/reads/keys()
          take key
          fork test, changed/has(key)
            hold
              save hit, true
              halt
        fork test, hit
          hold
            push(next-due, one)
      save due, next-due
      save round, add(round, 1)

  save proven, make list
  # a fixpoint that does not settle proves nothing
  fork test, not(settled)
    hold
      back proven
  walk tasks
    take one
    fork test, not(one/spent)
      hold
        proven-in(ctx, one, proven)
  back proven
